// Title: Failed sign-in brute force against one account
// Data source table: SigninLogs
// What it detects: Many failed sign-ins (wrong password or smart lockout) for the same account from the
//   same IP address inside one time bucket. This is the cloud equivalent of password guessing against a
//   single user.
// Likely false positives: A phone or mail client retrying with a stale saved password; a service or
//   automation account whose secret expired; a shared NAT or corporate egress IP where several people
//   mistype at once.
// MITRE ATT&CK technique: T1110.001 Brute Force: Password Guessing
// Tuning notes: Set failureThreshold from your tenant baseline. Buckets are tumbling, so a burst that
//   straddles a bucket edge can be split in two; as a scheduled analytics rule use a 10 minute frequency
//   and a 20 minute lookback. Exclude known egress IPs with a watchlist. ResultType 50126 means invalid
//   username or password, 50053 means the account is locked (smart lockout). SigninLogs holds interactive
//   sign-ins only; non-interactive ones are in AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs.
// Status: Written against the documented SigninLogs schema. Not yet run in a live Sentinel workspace.

let lookback = 1d;
let binSize = 10m;
let failureThreshold = 10;
let failureCodes = dynamic(["50126", "50053"]);
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| where ResultType in (failureCodes)
| summarize
    FailedAttempts = count(),
    FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated),
    LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated),
    Apps = make_set(AppDisplayName, 10),
    Countries = make_set(tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion), 5)
    by UserPrincipalName, IPAddress, TimeBucket = bin(TimeGenerated, binSize)
| where FailedAttempts >= failureThreshold
| project TimeBucket, UserPrincipalName, IPAddress, FailedAttempts, FirstSeen, LastSeen, Apps, Countries
| order by FailedAttempts desc
